hey guys this is your final month in the  90-day weight-loss challenge to a new  you firstly congratulate yourself for  getting to this point losing weight is  not easy and you have achieved a great  deal so enjoy your success you deserve  the very best for all the effort hard  work and time you have put in do you fit  better in your clothes do you feel  better about yourself  are you more energized and upbeat well  let's start the third month by  reevaluating your goal weight do you  still have 15 pounds or more to lose if  so continue on your current workout and  meal plan and be sure to increase your  workout intensity every four weeks to  challenge your muscles and keep burning  fat you can also get my month 3 workout  plan from my websites or are you at your  final 5 to 10 pounds and you're kind of  struggling to lose the last few pounds  I'll be sharing with you 10 tips to  break through your plateau when you go  on a weight loss journey at one point or  another you will hit a plateau where the  skill just stop moving this usually  happens when you get closer to your goal  firstly it's important to understand  that as you start losing weight your  overall metabolism decreases because  your body has to burn fewer calories to  control a smaller you  therefore the heavier you are the more  you burn the lighter you are the less  you burn the safe weight loss ratio is  between 1 to 2 pounds per week but as  you get closer to your goal expect to  only lose between 1/2 to 1 pound per  week  hence it takes much longer for a smaller  you to lose the last 5 to 10 pounds in  comparison to when you initially started  at a much heavier weight before I share  my tips with you I want you to reassess  your ideal weight and be honest  ask yourself if the magic number is  really the right weight for you perhaps  you have lost fat and gained muscles so  your new toned body is much healthier  and have  with few extra pounds on for instance  when I started working out my goal was  to be 45 kilos because that was my  weight in high school as I started  training I realized that I will never be  45 kilos again because of the additional  muscles I have so now I'm between 48 to  50 kilos but I am much smaller in frame  in comparison to when I was 45 kilos  basically more lean muscles and less  body fat another factor to consider is  once you have achieved your magic number  will you be able to maintain  approximately the same workout and diet  pace for the rest of your life I want  you to start thinking about your  maintaining strategy now so set a  sustainable life goal where you will be  able to sustain your new weight for life  I'm sure you know somebody who has lost  a lot of weight but several months down  the road he or she has put on 10 pounds  or more or this might has even happened  to you this is because you have only  been aiming for your weight goal but you  have not been aiming for your life goal  hence once you achieve your weight goal  you tend to let go and that's when the  weight starts to creep back on so I'm  going to share with you 10 tips to lose  the last 5 to 10 pounds and this is also  applicable to those of you who is  looking to maintain your weight so let's  start by looking at your workouts the  first tip is to workout less but intense  no matter what workout you do if you  were to increase the intensity you won't  burn more fat and you will lose weight  quicker so do interval trainings instead  of steady paced cardio increase the  weights you're using do explosive  movements like jump squats reduce your  rest time to burn more fat and to burn  more calories intensity is more  important than your workout length  spending only 20 to 30 minutes of  intense workout and giving it your  maximum effort is far more effective  than an hour long of moderate jogging  not only where you burn more fat during  the short period of time you will also  be burning more after your workout which  is no  as the afterburn the more intensive  workout is the greater the afterburn  effect your body will burn fat more  efficiently between 24 to 48 hours after  an intense workout so increase your  intensity tip number two is to switch  your workouts when your body is  accustomed to doing the same workout for  the past three to four months it will  not be as effective anymore  so try something completely different  when you force your body to adapt new  movements you will start burning again  for instance if you are used to running  four times weekly and you have a very  good stamina that does not mean you will  have the same stamina if you were to  start swimming so try to run twice  weekly and swim twice weekly instead or  even join a yoga class Pilates class  cycling or try boxing which is something  I'm currently doing at the moment some  of you have mentioned that I look leaner  nowadays and that's just by mixing up my  workout by adding one kickboxing session  a week I have seen and feel the  difference myself switching your  workouts will not only boost your  metabolic rate it will make your routine  feel fresh again it's motivating and  it's especially important if you are at  a maintenance stage so try something  completely different the third tip is to  strength train at least twice a week as  I've mentioned earlier as your body gets  smaller your metabolism will slow it  down and that is why losing the last few  pounds is so difficult metabolic rate is  directly linked to the amount of muscles  you have in your body the more lean  muscles you have the higher your resting  metabolic rate will be if you want to  tone up strength training is the way  those who do a lot of cardio with our  strength training can be slim but not  toned strength training will give you a  firmer physique and it will help to give  you a better posture so aim to do your  strength training and you can mix it up  with your cardio which is what most of  my workout videos are a combination of  strength training and cardio so 